WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.140
We can save the day.

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.020
We will stand our ground.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.000
We will be brave.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Brave.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.380
Brave [again]

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.300
We will be heard.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.000
We will matter.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:08.500
Matter.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.260
Matter [again]

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.360
Vote [6 times]

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.240
Nyeh

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.500
If you want to alienate almost anyone, no
matter their politics,

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.140
just say three little words:

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.260
Your friends will gasp, celebrities will judge
you,

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.900
your mother might still love you, but only
grudgingly.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.760
Tell the world that you care about what happens
to it.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.420
You have an obligation.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.400
For America.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.200
For America [repeated]

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.120
For America [tearing up]

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.940
Don't you care about America?

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.120
You not voting changes your life.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.440
You are dishonoring your family.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.800
If you don't vote, then you're an idiot.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.320
Don't buy the guilt trip.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.140
Not voting can be an equally legitimate and
moral choice.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.320
Here are four of the most common myths used
to shame non voters.

00:00:51.329 --> 00:00:53.250
We gotta stop thinking one vote.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.140
We can't say one vote doesn't matter.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:55.960
Your vote matters.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.140
It effects everything.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.340
First thing's first, you're not going to sway
a major election.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:04.900
A single vote has decided precisely zero federal
races in US history.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.760
And vanishingly few at the state level.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.280
Voting is like playing the power ball,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.300
punch your ticket or don't, your life is going
to stay the same.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.880
The last presidential election turned on fewer
than a hundred thousand votes.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.920
I know, but this is about you ans whether
or not you cast your one vote.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.800
It simply won't effect the outcome, not if
you live in a swing state,

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.060
not if the electoral college were abolished,

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.680
not even if you're in Florida and your chad
is hung like a moose.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.400
You can't complain if you didn't vote.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.980
Well he's gonna suck, well you didn't do anything
about it.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.920
Only about half the voting age population
makes it to the polls

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.560
and groups including young people, the poor
and the disabled

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.560
are underrepresented on voter rolls.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.000
Do they not deserve a voice?

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.479
The act of voting does not a good citizen
make

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.360
and it's actually one of the least effective
ways

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.500
you can contribute to the American experiment.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.140
Most social and cultural change happens outside
the political sphere

00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:51.540
and that's a good thing.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.560
Rather than follow the latest horse race,

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:56.390
you might spend your scarce time developing
a new vaccine,

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.000
exposing corruption or microwaving a burrito.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.600
Any of these things can have a greater tangible
impact on the world than your vote.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.860
I vote because it's all of our civic duty.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.659
People died for that right.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.520
I vote because I'm not a motherfucking communist.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.900
Generations of brave Americans have fought
for your right to vote

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.280
and for your right not to.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.640
In fact, you might choose not to vote because
you love your country.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:18.960
Maybe you don't feel educated

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.060
or at least not enough to cancel out the vote
of your well informed neighbor.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.500
That's ok and really quite moral.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.600
Besides, even the most knowledgeable voters

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.420
can't predict what a candidate will do once
in office.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.600
Look, a lot of our elected officials are uninformed.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:36.000
Remember when Obama was going to reign in
W's foreign adventuring?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.900
It was about 10 years and one drone kill list
ago.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.420
They should just vote because it matters you
know.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.940
Your employer can't tell you that you don't
have time.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.360
Just get out and vote.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.510
A principled citizen might actively avoid
a two party system

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.230
that systemically silences alternative voices.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.040
You might decide that it doesn't represent
your interests by design.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.940
That by voting for the lesser of two evils,

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.280
you're only helping the fat cats in Washington
maintain their smokescreen of legitimacy.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.700
Why on earth wouldn't you want to vote?

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.560
I think voting is great, I just didn't care
this time

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.000
because it was between a giant douche and
a turd sandwich.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.640
But Stan don't you know?

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.320
It's always between a giant douche and a turd
sandwich.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:15.320
If that's the case, you should feel free to
wash your hands of the whole rotten mess.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.680
At the end of the day, you might want to vote.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.240
Maybe to give your grand-daughter an up close
look at the machinery of American government.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.600
Maybe to get that fashion-forward sticker
selfie

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.840
that proves to all your instafriends how woke
or uncucked you are.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.560
I'm afraid I'm turning out because I wanna
impress my friends.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.140
Maybe you just really love middle school gyms.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.640
So this Tuesday, go ahead and rock the vote
if it makes you happy.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.720
But if you decide that it's a symbolic gesture

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.660
that's unlikely to tangibly help your family
or community,

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:48.020
it's ok to spend your time and resources doing
something more impactful.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.560
This Tuesday, it's ok not to vote.

